WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.101
♪ Wakanda Forever ♪

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:05.672
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.807
-You look gorgeous.
You look gorgeous here, too.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.342
Ooh-la-la.
Come on.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.409
-Thank you.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:11.644
-Thanks for coming back
to the show.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.046
Congrats on "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.948
The reviews have been fantastic.

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.117
This is giant.
-Yes, it is.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.285
-Yes.
-I feel it.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.352
-You do, right?
-I do.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:21.620
-Me, too, I feel it, as well.
Yeah.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.956
I want to ask you some questions
about filming the movie,

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.425
because there's a lot of it --
not -- no spoilers --

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:29.095
but there's a lot of it
that is underwater.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.296
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.497
-That's fair to say.
-I can say that, right?

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:32.499
Yeah, yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.066
-And a lot of that's real,
right?

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.568
You're -- it's not just CGI.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.837
-No, we actually worked
underwater.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.706
-I think that's -- I --
I mean, I can't act at all.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.108
[ Laughter ]
But acting underwater, I think,

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.376
would be a whole
nother level of bad.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.144
-It is a whole other level.
-What do you do?

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.912
How do you do
to practice or train?

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:52.385
-Well, before I did this film,
Ryan sent me a text saying,

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:56.155
"On a scale of 1 to 10,
how good can you swim?"

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.558
And I said,
"Mm, 4, if I'm lucky."

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.461
'Cause I swim -- I would swim
like a panicked puppy, you know?

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:03.629
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.266
And so I knew
I had to take some training.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.834
So I took some swimming
training, and --

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.136
but I also
did this thing called XPT.

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:14.540
That is
extreme performance training,

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.411
that was designed by Gabby Reece
and Laird Hamilton.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.779
-Laird Hamilton, sure.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:24.216
And it's learning how to
improve your breath capacity

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:26.686
by performing tasks underwater.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:31.690
So, I would carry these weights
and walk on the floor of a pool.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.092
-Yeah, and just
keep practicing that.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.526
You brought us video?
-I did.

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:36.595
-Which is very nice.
Here's Lupita training

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:38.531
underwater for "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.300 line:0%
Look at this.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.769 line:0%
-Wait.
Ooh.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:45.104 line:0%
No, that would freak me out.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.505 line:0%
-It's otherworldly, huh?

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.941 line:0%
-Yeah, because -- wow.
But that's --

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.476 line:0%
-But it's super serene
down there.

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.779
-It's kind of
a mental training, as well.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.246
-Oh, yeah, it's all about

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:57.283
overriding your panic button,
you know?

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.586
And 'cause you really have about
two minutes worth of air

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.922
inside you,
of oxygen inside you.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.991
So when you panic, you still
have two minutes to live.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:09.829
So it's about trying
to prolong that panic

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.897
so that you can do more
underwater.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.933
-Do you find yourself calmer
in just real life, in oxygen?

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.805
-You know, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.205
-Not underwater?

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:21.907
-No, it does transfer
to real life.

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.976
-It does, right?
-Yeah, because you have to just

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.079
find the calm inside you.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.014
So, it is --
it's definitely helped me

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:31.551
in situations of high stress,
to just zone in

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.953
and almost
go back into the womb.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.354
-Wow.
-That's the feeling, right?

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:36.923
Like, being surrounded by water.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.423
You were one of
the first actresses ever

00:02:38.423 --> 00:02:40.993
to get cast in "Black Panther."

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.729
Did -- Do -- Who did you
talk to when you got it?

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.999
And who knew that you got it,
and got the role and did --

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.067
Were you allowed to tell anyone,
or it's very secretive?

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.435
It's Marvel.
-Oh, no.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:53.239
I -- Oh, well,
so when I got the role,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:57.243
I didn't know what
the Black Panther was.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.544
I was not familiar
with the comic.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.779
[ Laughter ]
I'm from Kenya.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.480
I'm allowed, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.315
-Yeah, sure,
you're allowed, yeah.

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.418
-This wasn't my area.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.552
-And so --
-So, you just went

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:07.820
for a meeting with Marvel.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.455
-Yeah, I went
for a meeting with Marvel.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.656
They were interested in me.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.658
And then I found out
that Ryan Coogler

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.627
was doing this movie called
"Black Panther."

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.463
And so I hit up my friend
Bill DeMeritt, who is, like,

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.065
a big comic buff.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.101
I mean, he lives in comics.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.268
-And so I called him up.

00:03:23.268 --> 00:03:24.904
I'd gone to school with him,
drama school.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.905
And so, I called him up,
like, "Yo, is this thing called

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:30.243
'The Black Panther'
that I'm up for that --

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.812
And please just give me the --
the down low."

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.813
-Yeah, "Run me down.
What is it?"

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.947
-Yeah, like, "What is it?"

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.550
And so, he gave me,
like, full history.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.385
I mean, he is such a buff.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.720
I go to him every time
I'm doing anything with Marvel.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.923
-Did he freak out,
or was he like, "Wait.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.558
Ryan Coogler put --"
-Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.260
He freaked all the way out.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.362
He was so excited,
and he was like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.230
I'm gonna be living vicariously
through you."

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.032
[ Laughter ]
-No way.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.968
You know what I thought
was funny, too, last night?

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.502
We had Winston on the show.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.072
-Winston, who you actually
went to drama school with.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.473
-Yes, I did.
-And isn't that fun

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:02.642
to see each other, and you go,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.809
"Oh, we went to school
together"?

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.010
Now you're in
"Black Panther" together.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.312
-Yeah.
-Were you allowed to

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.847
tell each other, like, "Dude,
did you get the job?

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.281
I'm in it," or --
-Well, no.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:13.252
I had no idea. I didn't know
he was in it for a hot minute.

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:16.021
We had actually watched
"Avengers,"

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.658
the first "Avengers" together
right after we graduated.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.559
And I remember we were
in Brooklyn watching it,

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:22.628
and we're like, "Wow.
Wouldn't it be cool

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.130
to one day even just
be an extra on that film?"

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.365
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.400
-Wow, it's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.369
Look at you -- look at you now.
-Look at us now.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:34.073
-I love it!

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.542
Of course, everyone's talking
about Rihanna has a new song.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.910
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.945
-The first song in six years
that is on the soundtrack.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.613
It's coming out.
And I was like, "Oh, man.

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:43.449
It's gonna be fantastic."
-Yeah.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.951
-And here's a picture
of you guys.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.420
This went around the Internet.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.122
-That was the day I met her
for the first time,

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:52.625
and she was sitting next to me.
-Yeah.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.426
-I just -- that was a lot.

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:55.761
That was a lot.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.930
-This went all over the Internet
because everyone's like,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.899
"I want to see this movie."
-Yeah.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.233
[ Laughter ]
-Like, "What is this movie?"

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.802
Like, Rihanna is like --
what, is she a spy?

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.205
And what is going on?
Like, what is the movie there?

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:09.108
And they're like -- and then it
went all over the Internet.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.879
I think Ava --
-Ava Duvernay was supposed

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.179
to direct it and --
-She got it.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:16.282
-Issa Rae was gonna write it.
-Yes.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.650
-Yep, mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.419
So, it's still out there,
and it's still avail--

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.621
if Rihanna wants to do it.
-Hey, listen.

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:25.224
When she retires
from dominating the world,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.726
maybe she'll have time...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.727
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-...to make a movie like that.

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:33.466
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:36.302
-I can't imagine
how difficult the --

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:41.040
the filming of the movie was,
knowing about Chadwick Boseman

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.310
and losing Chadwick Boseman.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.347
He was on our show a bunch of
times, and we always loved him.

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:53.419
He was just such a kind and
sweet, a big personality guy.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.454
What do you remember
about Chadwick when you --

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.223
when you worked with him?
Any stories?

00:05:57.223 --> 00:06:00.426
-You know, Chadwick had --
he was -- he was very quiet.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.994
You know, like, he was --

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.897
He was also very funny.
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.901
-And quite the -- he could be
mischievous, as well.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:09.935
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:12.371
-But he was also
an eternal student.

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:15.475
I remember when we were
promoting the first

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:19.111
"Black Panther," we were all
on a plane to South Korea.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:22.482
We were the only ones
in first class, the whole cast,

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.983
and we were all in our pajamas,
and we were tired.

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:26.785
We'd been going a mile a minute.

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:29.621
And so, most of us were asleep.
And I woke up from a nap,

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:31.991
looked over,
and Chadwick was sitting there

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.394
with a dense history book.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.830
An African history book.
-Wow.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.932
-And I was like,
"Yo, Chadwick, right now?"

00:06:40.932 --> 00:06:42.134
[ Laughter ]
"Like, we're --

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.036
-"We're exhausted."
-"Yeah, we're exhausted.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.704
Why are you -- what --
what is that?"

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.740
Then he went on to tell me
what he was reading,

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.475
and he was just
an eternal student.

00:06:50.475 --> 00:06:51.710
He was so curious.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.613
He always wanted
to just sharpen his mind.

00:06:54.613 --> 00:06:58.518
And in so doing, he just
sharpened his understanding

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.319
of the human condition,
you know?

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.623
-The --
The movie is very emotional.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:06.425
But it's also -- I will say,
it's also very fun.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.526
It's a Marvel movie.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.395
It's a superhero movie.
It's got action.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.797
It's got everything you want
in a movie.

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.266
I mean, this one
knocks it out of the park.

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.634
I can't wait
for everyone to see it.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.736
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Lupita Nyong'o

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:19.371
in "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever."

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:20.639
Take a look.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:28.214
-When you lived without
saying a word, it hurts.

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:33.286
-How you re-create not being
there with all of you...

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:35.587
it was not easy.

00:07:35.587 --> 00:07:41.627
He was King
and Black Panther to everyone.

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:44.897
But to me...
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:53.172
...he was everything.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:55.707
My T'Challa.

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:57.742
-Lupita Nyong'o, everybody.

00:07:57.742 --> 00:08:00.179
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever"

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:02.614
is in theaters and IMAX
November 11th.

00:08:02.614 --> 00:08:03.916
Thank you so much.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.450
More "Tonight Show"
when we come back, everybody.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:06.285
Come on back.
[ Cheers and applause ]

